{
  "manufacturer": "Janitza",
  "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
  "model": "UMG 509-PRO power quality analyser (Modbus RTU / Modbus TCP)",
  "model_slug": "umg-509-pro",
  "short_model": "UMG 509-PRO",
  "aliases": [
    "UMG509-PRO",
    "UMG 509PRO",
    "UMG509PRO",
    "Janitza UMG 509"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power quality analyser)",
  "applies_to": "UMG 509-PRO per Modbus address list 1.059.004.2.n (06/2024).",
  "summary": "The UMG 509-PRO is a Janitza power quality analyser with a fourth voltage and current channel, an RS-485 port and network (IP) settings. Measurements are big-endian 32-bit floats; the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block is the same one used across Janitza meters. This map covers that block, the fourth channel, total power factor, consumed energy, digital I/O, transformer ratios and identity/network settings, with access rights as printed in the list.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (system time), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Power Analyser UMG 509-PRO - Modbus-address and Formulary",
    "doc_number": "1.059.004.2.n",
    "revision_date": "2024-06",
    "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG509-PRO/janitza-mal-umg509pro-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Transfer parameters, byte order p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; main values pp. 14-15; energy p. 26; other values pp. 30-32"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (high byte first, high word in the lower register = ABCD). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that mirror block is not listed.",
    "Float and integer values include the CT/VT ratios; short-format values do not. Only floats and 32-bit integers are used for measurements here.",
    "Access (R / RW) is copied from the list's RD/WR column.",
    "Left out: 19068 (consumed L1-L3 on tariff 1 only); the consumed total is at 13995 (_WH_V[4]).",
    "Left out: the energy delete commands 14141/14142 (_DEL_WH/_DEL_QH) because the list says '1 = delete' but marks them read-only (RD), so write access is unclear.",
    "Left out: RS-485 mode and baud rate (14328/14330), which have no value coding in the list, plus harmonics, min/max/mean blocks, display, PTP and password rows.",
    "Measured values refresh every 200 ms.",
    "The address list gives the serial framing and the IP/DHCP registers but does not name the Modbus TCP port; the port is left blank here."
  ],
